Lev is a vampire of [[Geography/Althane/Oresk/index|Oresk]] and a member of the [[Org/Althane/Oreskalka Cabal|Oreskalka Cabal]], whose seat is [[Geography/Althane/Oresk/Umbervale Hold|Umbervale Hold]]. He trained at the hold and left it with his sire, on terms bad enough that the family could put a contract out on him. He would like to lead the cabal himself, and has been told that would take allies inside the family rather than strength.

He is a [[Org/Althane/Golden Sparrows|Golden Sparrow]] and has done the movement's killing. He murdered a writer in his own home for writing against the Sparrows, and he has killed a man in a train station with a single pencil. He is practiced at disguise and at playing a part, and keeps a folding cane among the odds and ends in his bag so he can pass as an old man. He went openly in bat wings for a time, and now goes in another face with the wings away.

Lev once bound himself to [[Divinity/Unknown Entities/Nox|Nox]], offering his life and his service as its sword in exchange for the destruction of [[Divinity/Unknown Entities/The Deep|the creature from below]]. A strip of its black silk lay fused to his arm and his blade bled black. He traded that bond away, for the power to open a door anywhere the [[Divinity/Immix|Lighthouse]] reaches. He keeps the chrome of [[Geography/Syrin (Locality)|Syrin]] in his skull and neck.

He carries the still-beating heart of a dead blood relative, [[People/Althane/Xanthin Oreskalka|Xanthin Oreskalka]], and says he killed him.

He travels with [[People/Althane/Henrik|Henrik]], [[People/Althane/Divex|Divex]] and [[People/Althane/Dawnmonger|Dawnmonger]] as [[Org/Althane/The Weft|the Weft]].
